 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Who called the Ottoman Empire the sick man of Europe?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Russia's Tsar Nicholas the First, in 1853. He said a sick man. The words of Europe were added later."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Was it really sick?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1839",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It had lost Greece, and Egypt was almost independent. Many in Istanbul knew it had to change."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1839, a new sultan took the throne: Abdülmecid the First. He was sixteen.",
   "scene": "abdulmecid",
   "date": "1839",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "say": "In 1839, a new sultan took the throne: Abdul-mejid the First. He was sixteen."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That November, in Gülhane, the palace rose garden, his minister Mustafa Reşid Pasha read out a decree.",
   "scene": "resid",
   "date": "3 November 1839",
   "place": "Gülhane",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "say": "That November, in Gul-hane, the palace rose garden, his minister Mustafa Reshid Pasha read out a decree."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did it promise?",
   "scene": "edict",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Safety of life and property, fair taxes, fair military service, and the same rights for every faith."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It began the Tanzimat: the reorganisation.",
   "say": "It began the Tanzimaht: the reorganisation."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did it cure the sick man?",
   "scene": "crimea",
   "date": "1853",
   "place": "Black Sea"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. In 1853, Russia went to war again. But this time Britain and France fought on the Ottoman side, and they won."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The Crimean War gave the world one of its first great war photographs.",
   "scene": "fenton",
   "date": "1855",
   "place": "Crimea",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "And in Istanbul, at the barracks in Üsküdar, Florence Nightingale nursed the wounded. Her tower there is now a small museum.",
   "scene": "scutari",
   "date": "1854",
   "place": "Scutari",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   },
   "say": "And in Istanbul, at the barracks in Uskudar, Florence Nightingale nursed the wounded. Her tower there is now a small museum."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So things got better?",
   "scene": "berlin",
   "date": "1878",
   "place": "Berlin",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "For a while. But after another war with Russia, the Congress of Berlin in 1878 took away much of the Balkans."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did they lose?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1878",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Romania, Serbia and Montenegro became independent, Bulgaria self-governing. Austria took over Bosnia, and Britain took Cyprus."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Gallipoli, 1915. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: Gallipoli, 1915",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ]
}